SUMMARY:Russell Peters LIVE at Pittsburgh Improv
DTSTAMP:20260806T053906Z
DTSTART:20260806T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout Russell Peters\nRussell 
	Peters is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians in the world\, rec
	ently named by Rolling Stone as one of the 50 Best Comics of All Time. \nT
	he Toronto-born comedian started doing stand-up at age 19 and spent 15 yea
	rs honing his craft before his 2004 CTV special launched him to global sta
	rdom. He became the first comedian to sell out Toronto’s Air Canada Centre
	 and went on to break attendance records at Madison Square Garden\, the Sy
	dney Opera House\, and London’s O2 Arena. \nIn 2013\, Peters became the fi
	rst comedian to create a Netflix Original Comedy Special. His Relax* World
	 Tour (*It’s not that serious.) brings his signature observational humor a
	nd crowd work to stages across North America. \nEvent Details\nDate: Thurs
	day\, August 6\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM (doors open at 6:00 PM)\nVenue: Pitts
	burgh Improv\, 166 E. Bridge St\, Homestead\, PA 15120\nTour: Relax* World
	 Tour (*It’s not that serious.)\nAge Restriction: 21+ Event\nShow Duration
	: Approximately 90 minutes \nAbout the Venue\nThe Pittsburgh Improv is Pit
	tsburgh’s premier comedy club\, located in the Waterfront entertainment co
	mplex in Homestead\, PA — just minutes from downtown Pittsburgh. \nThe int
	imate showroom seats approximately 300 guests with excellent sightlines fr
	om every seat. A full-service bar and restaurant are on-site\, with a two-
	drink minimum per person. \nFree parking is available throughout the Water
	front complex. Easily accessible via I-376 and Route 837. Arrive early to 
	enjoy dinner before the show. \nWhat to Expect\nRussell Peters is famous f
	or his razor-sharp crowd work and his ability to turn any audience member 
	into comedy gold. No two shows are ever the same. \nExpect hilarious obser
	vations about culture\, race\, family\, and everyday life delivered with w
	orld-class timing. His ability to connect with diverse audiences has made 
	him one of the most beloved live performers in comedy history. \nThe Pitts
	burgh Improv typically features a local opener before the headliner takes 
	the stage. \nTicket Information\nTickets range from $30 – $75 depending on
	 seating and availability. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post co
	ntains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.\
	n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/russell-peters-live-at-pittsburgh-impr
	ov/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/russell-peters-live-at-pittsburgh-impr
	ov/
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Improv\, 166 E. Bridge St\, Homestead\, Pennsylvania\, 
	15120\, United States
