SUMMARY:Rene Vaca LIVE at Raleigh Improv
DTSTAMP:20260806T053907Z
DTSTART:20260807T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Perfor
	mer\nRene Vaca is a rising star in the world of stand-up comedy\, born and
	 raised in the San Fernando Valley of Southern California. His journey to 
	the stage is as compelling as his comedy — after his father was incarcerat
	ed\, Vaca started his own landscaping business at just 15 years old to sup
	port himself. He later earned acceptance to the University of California\,
	 Merced\, where he began pursuing his true passion: making people laugh. \
	nVaca’s hard work paid off in a big way when he won the prestigious 16th A
	nnual StandUp NBC competition\, one of the most respected comedy competiti
	ons in the country. Since then\, he has shared the stage with comedy legen
	ds including Bill Burr\, Ken Jeong\, Amir K.\, and Jamie Kennedy. His 2025
	 Netflix special Live in Portland introduced him to millions of new fans\,
	 and his social media presence — with over 2 million followers — continues
	 to grow rapidly. \nKnown for his fearless crowd work\, sharp personal sto
	rytelling\, and clean callbacks that land with explosive energy\, Rene Vac
	a delivers a show that feels both intimate and electric. His comedy draws 
	from real life — his upbringing\, his hustle\, and his unique perspective 
	as a first-generation college graduate who made it on his own terms. \nEve
	nt Details\n\nDate: Friday\, August 7\, 2026\nShow Time: 7:00 PM EDT\nDoor
	s Open: 5:30 PM EDT\nVenue: Raleigh Improv\nAddress: 1224 Parkside Main St
	\, Cary\, NC 27519\nAge Restriction: 21+ (Valid ID required)\nSeating: Gen
	eral Admission\, first-come first-served (except groups and premium booths
	)\nNote: Two-item minimum purchase per person in the showroom. No cell pho
	nes\, photography\, or video recording during the performance.\n\nAbout th
	e Venue\nThe Raleigh Improv is the Triangle area’s premier comedy club\, l
	ocated at 1224 Parkside Main St in Cary\, NC — just minutes from downtown 
	Raleigh. Part of the nationally recognized Improv Comedy Club chain\, the 
	Raleigh Improv has hosted some of the biggest names in stand-up comedy and
	 continues to be the go-to destination for world-class comedy in the Resea
	rch Triangle. \nThe venue features a classic comedy club layout with a mai
	n showroom that offers excellent sightlines from every seat. The intimate 
	atmosphere ensures that no matter where you sit\, you’ll feel close to the
	 action. The club offers a full food and beverage menu\, with a mandatory 
	two-item minimum per guest — making it a perfect dinner-and-a-show experie
	nce. Premium booth seating is available for groups looking for a more elev
	ated experience\, complete with food and beverage credits. \nThe Raleigh I
	mprov is conveniently located in the Parkside Town Commons shopping center
	 in Cary\, with ample free parking available in the surrounding lot. The v
	enue is easily accessible from I-40 and US-1\, making it a convenient dest
	ination for comedy fans from Raleigh\, Durham\, Chapel Hill\, and the surr
	ounding Research Triangle area. \nWhat to Expect\nRene Vaca’s live show is
	 a high-energy\, crowd-interactive experience that blends personal storyte
	lling with sharp observational humor. Expect Vaca to work the room with hi
	s signature fearless crowd work — he’s known for turning audience interact
	ions into some of the funniest moments of the night. His set weaves togeth
	er stories from his upbringing in the San Fernando Valley\, his entreprene
	urial hustle\, and his rapid rise in the comedy world. \nThis is a solo he
	adlining show\, so you’ll get a full set from Rene Vaca himself. The show 
	runs approximately 90 minutes to two hours. Given the 21+ age restriction\
	, this is an adults-only evening of comedy — arrive early to grab a drink\
	, find your seat\, and settle in before the laughs begin. Doors open at 5:
	30 PM\, giving you plenty of time to enjoy the full club experience before
	 the 7:00 PM showtime. \nFans of comedians like Bill Burr\, Bert Kreischer
	\, and Felipe Esparza will feel right at home with Rene Vaca’s style — raw
	\, honest\, and genuinely funny. This is one of the hottest up-and-coming 
	comedians in the country\, and catching him at an intimate venue like the 
	Raleigh Improv is a rare opportunity. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $
	25 – $75 (plus fees) \n\nGA Ticket: $25 (+ fees)\nGA Booth for 4: $75/pers
	on (includes $200 food & beverage credit)\nVIP Meet & Greet Ticket: $70 (+
	 fees)\nPremium Booth for 4: $90/person (includes $200 food & beverage cre
	dit)\n\nTickets are available through the official Ticketmaster/TicketWeb 
	link below. Note: The Raleigh Improv strictly prohibits ticket resale — pu
	rchase only through official channels. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \n
	This post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra c
	ost to you.\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/rene-vaca-live-at-raleigh-
	improv/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/rene-vaca-live-at-raleigh-improv/
LOCATION:Raleigh Improv\, 1224 Parkside Main St\, Cary\, NC\, 27519\, Unite
	d States Of America
